{"uid":"include/secure_fetch.h::sf_global_init","name":"sf_global_init","qualname":"sf_global_init","kind":"function","file":"include/secure_fetch.h","line":227,"end_line":227,"language":"h","signature":"void sf_global_init(void);","params":[],"returns":"void","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Initialises process-global transport state (libcurl/OpenSSL) once, from the main thread, before any concurrent sf_get/sf_post. libcurl's implicit init on first use is NOT thread-safe, so an orchestrator that fetches from worker threads MUST call this first.","description":"Idempotent; safe to call more than once. A single-threaded caller need not call it. There is intentionally no cleanup: it would race in-flight fetches at shutdown, and the OS reclaims everything on exit.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/secure_fetch.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
